title: "Agri-SDSS"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 2.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23369081
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeremie-durand/Agri-SDSS"
abstract: >-
  Agri-SDSS is an open-source web platform for sustainable agriculture
  research in Quebec, developed within the MOS project supported by the
  RQRAD. It brings together public data that used to be scattered: farm
  parcels and crops, soil maps, weather, climate and satellite imagery. The
  data, and the calculations run on demand (for example a parcel's NDVI from
  satellite imagery, or its mean elevation from lidar), are served through
  APIs that follow open international standards (OGC API, STAC), so other
  software, platforms and research teams can reuse them in their own tools.
  On the interactive map, clicking a parcel returns its portrait with several
  agronomic variables computed automatically, and an experimental AI
  assistant answers questions about the data in natural language. A first
  soil organic matter prediction model is offered as a proof of concept for
  436 fields in southern Quebec; the platform is designed to host the future
  model of soil organic matter accumulation potential. Agri-SDSS is modular:
  independent blocks (data pipeline, APIs, interactive map, AI assistant) can
  each be updated, replaced or reused on their own.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - spatial decision support system
  - sustainable agriculture
  - soil organic matter
  - STAC
  - OGC API
  - Quebec
